.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-org 1  "taurctl-org " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-org \- Manage organizations and member roles
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl org\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage organizations and member roles
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taurctl\-org\-list(1)
Organizations you belong to
.TP
taurctl\-org\-create(1)
Create an organization (you become Owner)
.TP
taurctl\-org\-show(1)
Show members and roles
.TP
taurctl\-org\-delete(1)
Delete an organization (Owner only)
.TP
taurctl\-org\-add\-member(1)
Add a member (Owner/Admin)
.TP
taurctl\-org\-set\-role(1)
Change a member\*(Aqs role (owner, admin, contributor)
.TP
taurctl\-org\-remove\-member(1)
Remove a member
.TP
taurctl\-org\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
